// Gives the root project the entry point named by its `--entry` argument, so the ghūl VS Code
// extension has a well-formed project to load every task's source into. Nothing runs it: the root
// project builds as a library, and each task under tasks/ is a program in its own right. Build and
// run tasks individually, from their own folders.

root_entry() =>
    IO.Std.write_line("Run each task on its own, for example: dotnet run --project tasks/hello-world-text")
